>
  <p><strong>Discover → execute → trace</strong> is the value loop. Not “WASM as a headline,” and not a count of governing specs. Find a reviewed capability, run the known artifact, keep evidence of what happened.</p>

  <h2>Discover</h2>
  <p>Look up a versioned capability by contract metadata — name, schema, risk, placement — not by regenerating business logic from a prompt. Public surfaces include the registry catalog, MCP search tools, and the skill path that checks the registry before authoring anything new. If the rule already exists, reuse it.</p>

  <h2>Execute</h2>
  <p>Run that exact artifact under the shared <code>runtime.wasm</code>. Preconditions and postconditions validate inputs and outputs. The sandbox isolates the call. Language SDKs, the CLI, and MCP are clients that ask the runtime to execute — they are not separate Traverses. See <a href="/questions/what-is-one-shared-runtime-wasm.html">What is one shared runtime.wasm?</a>.</p>

  <h2>Trace</h2>
  <p>Every run leaves a trace artifact: what was called, which contract version, the inputs and outputs that passed validation, and the outcome (including deny). Auditors and operators can replay the decision without re-deriving the rule. See <a href="/questions/what-is-a-trace-artifact.html">What is a trace artifact?</a>.</p>

  <h2>The agent proposes; the runtime decides</h2>
  <p>An agent can search, plan, and suggest a call. It does not get to invent the authoritative business answer. The runtime validates and either executes or denies. The public scene for that boundary: <a href="/blog/agent-freestyle-blocked.html">The agent freestyled a $2.4M wire. The runtime said no.</a> Runnable copy: <a href="/questions/how-do-i-run-the-agent-blocked-weekly-demo.html">how to run the weekly demo</a>.</p>

  <h2>What this is not</h2>
  <p>It is not a pitch about how many specs are approved. Specs and CI gates keep the codebase honest — cite them in footnotes or About, not as the product. For a citeable snapshot of what ships today, start at <a href="/what-is-real-today.html">what is real today</a>.</p>
</QuestionLayout>
